    "limitations": [
      "One end-to-end run per revision on this machine. These are comparative observations, not a portable frame-rate guarantee or a statistically repeated benchmark.",
      "The collection grew from 9 to 18 products. Scroll measurements compare the actual old and new showcase, not scenes normalized to identical content or scroll range. Baseline scroll range was not recorded.",
      "The main before/after comparison retains medium cards. The final website uses large cards so the 18-product catalog does not display more models simultaneously than the 16-instance runtime budget; its verification is recorded separately.",
      "In the medium-card comparison the runtime held 16 actors for 18 cards, leaving two card posters visible. Those estimates therefore describe the observed bounded working set, not all 18 models resident simultaneously.",
      "Navigation elapsed time includes routing, preparation and deliberate settling waits; it is not the configured animation duration.",
      "Estimated resident bytes describe the asset manager estimate, not measured process memory or exact GPU VRAM.",
      "The DOM snapshot microbenchmark below disables WebGPU and measures only header cloning/style capture. It is separate from complete navigation and GPU work."
